1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,257
Before one single Pagani Utopia reached a

2
00:00:03,257 --> 00:00:07,547
customer, the company built eight complete prototypes,

3
00:00:07,547 --> 00:00:09,136
twelve scale models,

4
00:00:09,136 --> 00:00:11,678
and spent more than six years on

5
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:12,631
the project.

6
00:00:12,811 --> 00:00:15,834
Three of those prototypes existed only to

7
00:00:15,834 --> 00:00:17,014
test the engine,

8
00:00:17,014 --> 00:00:18,488
for about two years.

9
00:00:18,668 --> 00:00:20,979
And the result is a car that,

10
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,970
by its maker's own words,

11
00:00:22,970 --> 00:00:26,077
has no hybrid system and no dual-clutch

12
00:00:26,077 --> 00:00:26,714
gearbox.

13
00:00:26,894 --> 00:00:28,346
This is the Pagani Utopia,

14
00:00:28,346 --> 00:00:30,190
and there are two things about it

15
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:31,921
that you probably did not know.

16
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:34,668
The first is about a gearbox that

17
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:37,356
almost nobody asked a carmaker for in

18
00:00:37,356 --> 00:00:38,809
the twenty twenties,

19
00:00:38,809 --> 00:00:41,060
and why Pagani built it anyway.

20
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:43,545
The second is about what is hiding

21
00:00:43,545 --> 00:00:45,443
inside the carbon structure,

22
00:00:45,443 --> 00:00:48,019
where one car contains more than forty

23
00:00:48,019 --> 00:00:50,052
different recipes of material.

24
00:00:50,232 --> 00:00:52,812
Both are verified in published sources,

25
00:00:52,812 --> 00:00:54,598
and we will show you where.

26
00:00:54,948 --> 00:00:57,203
Every fact in this video comes from

27
00:00:57,203 --> 00:01:00,102
published sources, listed in the description.

28
00:01:00,282 --> 00:01:02,011
Where sources disagree,

29
00:01:02,011 --> 00:01:03,289
we will tell you.

30
00:01:03,469 --> 00:01:05,604
Where we do the maths ourselves,

31
00:01:05,604 --> 00:01:06,604
we will say so.

32
00:01:06,784 --> 00:01:08,456
Let us begin with the car.

33
00:01:08,806 --> 00:01:12,346
Wikipedia says the Pagani Utopia was unveiled

34
00:01:12,346 --> 00:01:14,549
on the twelfth of September,

35
00:01:14,549 --> 00:01:17,854
twenty twenty-two, at the Teatro Lirico in

36
00:01:17,854 --> 00:01:18,326
Milan.

37
00:01:18,506 --> 00:01:20,539
It is Pagani's third model,

38
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:22,873
after the Zonda and the Huayra,

39
00:01:22,873 --> 00:01:25,133
and it is built in San Cesario

40
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:26,714
sul Panaro, in Italy.

41
00:01:26,894 --> 00:01:28,897
Its internal code is C ten,

42
00:01:28,897 --> 00:01:31,419
following the C eight of the Zonda

43
00:01:31,419 --> 00:01:33,570
and the C nine of the Huayra.

44
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,209
The engine is a five point nine

45
00:01:36,209 --> 00:01:40,050
eight litre Mercedes-AMG twin-turbocharged V twelve.

46
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:44,527
Wikipedia lists eight hundred sixty-four metric horsepower

47
00:01:44,527 --> 00:01:46,158
at six thousand r p m,

48
00:01:46,158 --> 00:01:49,344
and eleven hundred newton-metres of torque,

49
00:01:49,344 --> 00:01:52,901
available between two thousand eight hundred and

50
00:01:52,901 --> 00:01:55,346
five thousand nine hundred r p m.

51
00:01:55,526 --> 00:01:59,009
The engine alone weighs two hundred sixty-two

52
00:01:59,009 --> 00:02:00,170
kilograms, dry.

53
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,383
It is a rear mid-engine,

54
00:02:02,383 --> 00:02:04,014
rear-wheel-drive car.

55
00:02:04,194 --> 00:02:06,616
The dry weight is one thousand two

56
00:02:06,616 --> 00:02:08,397
hundred eighty kilograms.

57
00:02:08,577 --> 00:02:10,017
By our own arithmetic,

58
00:02:10,017 --> 00:02:12,898
the engine is therefore about twenty percent

59
00:02:12,898 --> 00:02:14,010
of the whole car.

60
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:17,314
Wikipedia lists the length at four thousand

61
00:02:17,314 --> 00:02:21,091
five hundred ninety-seven millimetres and the height

62
00:02:21,091 --> 00:02:23,924
at one thousand one hundred sixty-nine,

63
00:02:23,924 --> 00:02:25,232
a low, wide shape.

64
00:02:25,582 --> 00:02:28,643
Top Gear reports that only ninety-nine coupés

65
00:02:28,643 --> 00:02:29,596
will be built,

66
00:02:29,596 --> 00:02:32,181
at around two point two million pounds

67
00:02:32,181 --> 00:02:34,630
each, and that they were all already

68
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:35,311
allocated.

69
00:02:35,491 --> 00:02:38,439
Wikipedia says the first car was delivered

70
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:40,614
in October twenty twenty-three,

71
00:02:40,614 --> 00:02:43,282
with pricing starting at two point one

72
00:02:43,282 --> 00:02:44,755
nine million dollars.

73
00:02:45,106 --> 00:02:48,209
Supercar Blondie quoted the starting price as

74
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:51,519
two million, one hundred seventy thousand euros,

75
00:02:51,519 --> 00:02:54,347
just under two point two million dollars.

76
00:02:54,527 --> 00:02:56,666
So the sources differ a little,

77
00:02:56,666 --> 00:02:58,115
by currency and date.

78
00:02:58,295 --> 00:02:59,748
In every one of them,

79
00:02:59,748 --> 00:03:01,824
the Utopia is a car that costs

80
00:03:01,824 --> 00:03:04,039
about as much as a luxury house,

81
00:03:04,039 --> 00:03:06,600
and that was spoken for before anyone

82
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,223
drove it.

83
00:03:07,573 --> 00:03:09,349
Compare it with the car it replaced.

84
00:03:09,529 --> 00:03:12,089
The Huayra, according to Wikipedia,

85
00:03:12,089 --> 00:03:15,089
had a six litre twin-turbo Mercedes-AMG V

86
00:03:15,089 --> 00:03:18,674
twelve with seven hundred forty metric horsepower

87
00:03:18,674 --> 00:03:20,941
and one thousand newton-metres.

88
00:03:21,121 --> 00:03:22,703
By our own arithmetic,

89
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:26,082
the Utopia's eight hundred sixty-four is almost

90
00:03:26,082 --> 00:03:28,167
seventeen percent more power,

91
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:31,259
and its eleven hundred newton-metres is ten

92
00:03:31,259 --> 00:03:32,697
percent more torque.

93
00:03:33,047 --> 00:03:35,407
Top Gear says the new engine revs

94
00:03:35,407 --> 00:03:37,982
higher and is more flexible than the

95
00:03:37,982 --> 00:03:39,269
one it supersedes.

96
00:03:39,449 --> 00:03:41,470
The torque figure supports that.

97
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:45,022
Wikipedia says the eleven hundred newton-metres is

98
00:03:45,022 --> 00:03:48,259
available between two thousand eight hundred and

99
00:03:48,259 --> 00:03:50,485
five thousand nine hundred r p m.

100
00:03:50,665 --> 00:03:52,002
By our arithmetic,

101
00:03:52,002 --> 00:03:54,230
that is a band more than three

102
00:03:54,230 --> 00:03:55,715
thousand r p m wide.

103
00:03:56,066 --> 00:03:58,666
The timeline is also unusual.

104
00:03:58,846 --> 00:04:02,365
Wikipedia gives the unveiling as September twenty

105
00:04:02,365 --> 00:04:05,525
twenty-two and the first delivery as October

106
00:04:05,525 --> 00:04:06,962
twenty twenty-three.

107
00:04:07,142 --> 00:04:08,791
By our own arithmetic,

108
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:10,590
that is thirteen months.

109
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:14,296
And Pagani unveiled the roadster only twenty-two

110
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:15,986
months after the coupé,

111
00:04:15,986 --> 00:04:17,970
in July twenty twenty-four,

112
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:20,836
with a hundred thirty examples planned.

113
00:04:21,186 --> 00:04:23,015
Now the first thing you probably did

114
00:04:23,015 --> 00:04:23,473
not know.

115
00:04:23,653 --> 00:04:27,316
Wikipedia says the Utopia was developed over

116
00:04:27,316 --> 00:04:28,982
more than six years.

117
00:04:29,162 --> 00:04:30,270
In that time,

118
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:33,597
Pagani built eight complete prototypes.

119
00:04:33,777 --> 00:04:36,013
Three of them were used for about

120
00:04:36,013 --> 00:04:38,316
two years of engine testing alone.

121
00:04:38,496 --> 00:04:41,535
Imagine building three entire cars just so

122
00:04:41,535 --> 00:04:43,488
one engine could be tested.

123
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:47,559
Wikipedia says the team also made twelve

124
00:04:47,559 --> 00:04:51,279
scale models: ten at one-fifth scale and

125
00:04:51,279 --> 00:04:52,860
two at full size.

126
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:56,415
Supercar Blondie adds that the design process

127
00:04:56,415 --> 00:04:58,740
involved thousands of sketches.

128
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,849
So before the Utopia existed as a

129
00:05:01,849 --> 00:05:04,334
car, it existed as a pile of

130
00:05:04,334 --> 00:05:07,530
drawings and a small fleet of models

131
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:09,926
in clay or other materials.

132
00:05:10,277 --> 00:05:11,790
By our own arithmetic,

133
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:13,098
there is a pattern.

134
00:05:13,278 --> 00:05:17,152
Eight prototypes for ninety-nine coupés is roughly

135
00:05:17,152 --> 00:05:20,639
one prototype for every twelve customer cars.

136
00:05:20,819 --> 00:05:23,734
A mass-market car maker would need to

137
00:05:23,734 --> 00:05:26,728
build hundreds of thousands of cars to

138
00:05:26,728 --> 00:05:28,226
justify that ratio.

139
00:05:28,406 --> 00:05:30,356
Pagani needs ninety-nine.

140
00:05:30,707 --> 00:05:31,833
Why so many?

141
00:05:32,013 --> 00:05:34,521
Top Gear says Pagani's brief was to

142
00:05:34,521 --> 00:05:36,384
re-engage with simplicity,

143
00:05:36,384 --> 00:05:39,106
lightness and the pleasure of driving.

144
00:05:39,286 --> 00:05:42,572
The company says the engine meets California's

145
00:05:42,572 --> 00:05:44,000
emissions rules too.

146
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,302
So the engineers had to make a

147
00:05:46,302 --> 00:05:49,132
twin-turbo V twelve that is clean enough

148
00:05:49,132 --> 00:05:51,961
for California, light enough for Pagani,

149
00:05:51,961 --> 00:05:54,720
and exciting enough for a three million

150
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:55,639
dollar buyer.

151
00:05:55,989 --> 00:05:59,171
Top Gear quotes Horacio Pagani saying there

152
00:05:59,171 --> 00:06:01,836
are no heavy batteries and no hybrid

153
00:06:01,836 --> 00:06:04,278
power, just a wonderful V twelve.

154
00:06:04,458 --> 00:06:07,378
In an age when almost every hypercar

155
00:06:07,378 --> 00:06:09,082
adds electric motors,

156
00:06:09,082 --> 00:06:10,542
that was a choice.

157
00:06:10,722 --> 00:06:12,939
And the choice was not an accident.

158
00:06:13,119 --> 00:06:15,110
It was a six-year decision,

159
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:17,101
tested on three prototypes.

160
00:06:17,452 --> 00:06:20,868
The Wikipedia page also says the suspension

161
00:06:20,868 --> 00:06:23,727
is forged aluminium double-wishbone,

162
00:06:23,727 --> 00:06:27,382
based on experience from the track-only Huayra

163
00:06:27,382 --> 00:06:27,541
R.

164
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:29,917
So even the road car borrows from

165
00:06:29,917 --> 00:06:32,113
a car that never touched a public

166
00:06:32,113 --> 00:06:32,446
road.

167
00:06:32,626 --> 00:06:35,793
Racing knowledge flows into the Utopia through

168
00:06:35,793 --> 00:06:36,620
the chassis.

169
00:06:36,970 --> 00:06:40,139
Pagani's own roadster press release goes further.

170
00:06:40,319 --> 00:06:43,527
It says the eight suspension triangles are

171
00:06:43,527 --> 00:06:46,658
forged in aircraft-grade aluminium alloy.

172
00:06:46,838 --> 00:06:49,111
Eight triangles, four wheels,

173
00:06:49,111 --> 00:06:50,600
two on each corner.

174
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:53,015
That is a lot of expensive metal

175
00:06:53,015 --> 00:06:55,600
for parts most owners will never see,

176
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,627
and it is typical of how this

177
00:06:57,627 --> 00:06:58,675
company thinks.

178
00:06:59,025 --> 00:07:01,277
Weight was always Pagani's obsession.

179
00:07:01,457 --> 00:07:03,842
The Attic Capital summary of an interview

180
00:07:03,842 --> 00:07:05,995
quotes Horacio Pagani saying he has a

181
00:07:05,995 --> 00:07:06,751
weight mania.

182
00:07:06,931 --> 00:07:07,832
It tells how,

183
00:07:07,832 --> 00:07:10,050
when he first put the Mercedes V

184
00:07:10,050 --> 00:07:12,407
twelve for the Zonda on the scale,

185
00:07:12,407 --> 00:07:15,319
it weighed seventy kilograms less than the

186
00:07:15,319 --> 00:07:18,715
Lamborghini Diablo engine he had designed around.

187
00:07:18,895 --> 00:07:20,411
Twenty years later,

188
00:07:20,411 --> 00:07:22,007
the habit is intact.

189
00:07:22,357 --> 00:07:23,970
Now to the gearbox.

190
00:07:24,150 --> 00:07:27,859
Wikipedia says the Utopia has a seven-speed

191
00:07:27,859 --> 00:07:30,964
Xtrac gearbox, mounted transversely,

192
00:07:30,964 --> 00:07:33,551
offered as a pure manual or an

193
00:07:33,551 --> 00:07:35,017
automated manual.

194
00:07:35,197 --> 00:07:38,565
It pairs with an electro-mechanical differential through

195
00:07:38,565 --> 00:07:39,888
a triple-plate clutch.

196
00:07:40,068 --> 00:07:41,048
In plain words,

197
00:07:41,048 --> 00:07:43,009
you can have three pedals in a

198
00:07:43,009 --> 00:07:45,884
car with more than eight hundred horsepower.

199
00:07:46,235 --> 00:07:49,196
Supercar Blondie says it is a special

200
00:07:49,196 --> 00:07:52,317
seven-speed unit made by Xtrac just for

201
00:07:52,317 --> 00:07:54,478
this car, in both versions.

202
00:07:54,658 --> 00:07:57,116
And it quotes why Pagani built the

203
00:07:57,116 --> 00:08:00,443
manual: offering one was especially important,

204
00:08:00,443 --> 00:08:03,191
because it is what customers demanded.

205
00:08:03,371 --> 00:08:05,922
So the manual is not nostalgia from

206
00:08:05,922 --> 00:08:06,796
the company.

207
00:08:06,976 --> 00:08:08,800
It is an answer to the people

208
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,995
paying for the car.

209
00:08:10,345 --> 00:08:12,560
Top Gear adds another detail,

210
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,164
with a bit of humour.

211
00:08:14,344 --> 00:08:16,911
The article says there will be no

212
00:08:16,911 --> 00:08:20,178
virtual manual, and it quotes the company:

213
00:08:20,178 --> 00:08:21,889
no dual-clutch system,

214
00:08:21,889 --> 00:08:25,233
just a pure seven-speed manual or automated

215
00:08:25,233 --> 00:08:26,245
transmission.

216
00:08:26,425 --> 00:08:28,182
The automated version,

217
00:08:28,182 --> 00:08:29,300
Top Gear says,

218
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:32,575
is lighter, more compact and uses helical

219
00:08:32,575 --> 00:08:33,054
gears.

220
00:08:33,234 --> 00:08:34,824
It is not a dual-clutch.

221
00:08:35,175 --> 00:08:39,029
That matters because almost every modern hypercar

222
00:08:39,029 --> 00:08:41,153
uses a dual-clutch gearbox,

223
00:08:41,153 --> 00:08:43,906
which changes gear in a fraction of

224
00:08:43,906 --> 00:08:44,614
a second.

225
00:08:44,794 --> 00:08:47,240
Pagani chose neither that nor a hybrid

226
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:47,626
motor.

227
00:08:47,806 --> 00:08:50,227
By our reading of the sources,

228
00:08:50,227 --> 00:08:52,728
it chose the opposite approach:

229
00:08:52,728 --> 00:08:54,584
fewer parts, more feel,

230
00:08:54,584 --> 00:08:57,408
and an engine that stays in charge.

231
00:08:57,758 --> 00:09:01,233
The roadster press release describes the clutch

232
00:09:01,233 --> 00:09:03,008
as light and adjustable,

233
00:09:03,008 --> 00:09:04,561
a triple-disc clutch.

234
00:09:04,741 --> 00:09:07,003
That is an engineering answer to a

235
00:09:07,003 --> 00:09:07,934
human problem.

236
00:09:08,114 --> 00:09:10,455
A clutch that is too heavy would

237
00:09:10,455 --> 00:09:13,381
make an expensive car tiring in traffic,

238
00:09:13,381 --> 00:09:15,649
and one that is too light would

239
00:09:15,649 --> 00:09:16,380
feel numb.

240
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:18,828
Pagani says it made the pedal light

241
00:09:18,828 --> 00:09:19,799
and adjustable.

242
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:21,775
Now compare it with the Zonda.

243
00:09:21,955 --> 00:09:24,768
Wikipedia lists the Zonda Cinque of two

244
00:09:24,768 --> 00:09:28,158
thousand nine with a six-speed automated manual

245
00:09:28,158 --> 00:09:31,475
that shifts in under one hundred milliseconds.

246
00:09:31,655 --> 00:09:34,500
The Utopia goes back to the manual

247
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,508
idea, with seven speeds.

248
00:09:36,688 --> 00:09:38,294
Sixteen years apart,

249
00:09:38,294 --> 00:09:41,667
Pagani used the same gearbox philosophy in

250
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:43,434
an opposite direction.

251
00:09:43,784 --> 00:09:45,886
The Zonda C twelve itself,

252
00:09:45,886 --> 00:09:47,746
according to Wikipedia,

253
00:09:47,746 --> 00:09:50,900
came out in nineteen ninety-nine with a

254
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,165
six litre Mercedes V twelve.

255
00:09:53,345 --> 00:09:55,175
So the Utopia's engine,

256
00:09:55,175 --> 00:09:56,846
at nearly six litres,

257
00:09:56,846 --> 00:10:00,426
shows the same family idea twenty-three years

258
00:10:00,426 --> 00:10:04,564
later, now twin-turbocharged and built specially for

259
00:10:04,564 --> 00:10:06,951
Pagani, according to Top Gear.

260
00:10:07,302 --> 00:10:09,122
There is a second reason that the

261
00:10:09,122 --> 00:10:09,949
manual matters.

262
00:10:10,129 --> 00:10:13,282
Wikipedia says the Utopia is rear-wheel drive

263
00:10:13,282 --> 00:10:16,085
with an electro-mechanical differential.

264
00:10:16,265 --> 00:10:18,278
With no front motor to help,

265
00:10:18,278 --> 00:10:21,946
all eight hundred sixty-four horsepower reaches the

266
00:10:21,946 --> 00:10:24,032
road through the rear wheels.

267
00:10:24,212 --> 00:10:25,992
A car like that is a very

268
00:10:25,992 --> 00:10:28,982
direct machine, and a manual gearbox makes

269
00:10:28,982 --> 00:10:30,121
it even more so.

270
00:10:30,471 --> 00:10:32,400
We should be honest about what the

271
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,478
sources do not say.

272
00:10:33,658 --> 00:10:36,492
Top Gear's launch article does not give

273
00:10:36,492 --> 00:10:39,109
an acceleration time or a top speed,

274
00:10:39,109 --> 00:10:41,798
and the Wikipedia page for the Utopia

275
00:10:41,798 --> 00:10:42,597
lists none.

276
00:10:42,777 --> 00:10:44,426
So we do not quote any.

277
00:10:44,606 --> 00:10:47,261
Pagani has not published a number that

278
00:10:47,261 --> 00:10:48,240
we could find,

279
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,406
and we will not repeat a figure

280
00:10:50,406 --> 00:10:52,083
from a forum or a video.

281
00:10:52,433 --> 00:10:53,861
Now the second thing.

282
00:10:54,041 --> 00:10:57,448
Pagani's roadster press release says there are

283
00:10:57,448 --> 00:11:01,078
over forty formulas of composite materials within

284
00:11:01,078 --> 00:11:02,411
the same hypercar.

285
00:11:02,591 --> 00:11:03,660
Read that again.

286
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,059
Not forty parts.

287
00:11:05,239 --> 00:11:06,992
Forty different recipes.

288
00:11:07,172 --> 00:11:08,901
Each one mixes fibres,

289
00:11:08,901 --> 00:11:11,888
resins and layers in a particular way,

290
00:11:11,888 --> 00:11:15,425
to give a particular combination of strength,

291
00:11:15,425 --> 00:11:17,075
weight and stiffness.

292
00:11:17,425 --> 00:11:20,953
The same release names two of them:

293
00:11:20,953 --> 00:11:24,381
Carbo-Titanium HP sixty-two G two,

294
00:11:24,381 --> 00:11:27,305
and Carbo-Triax HP sixty-two.

295
00:11:27,485 --> 00:11:30,456
Carbo-titanium is Pagani's own name for a

296
00:11:30,456 --> 00:11:33,499
carbon fibre material woven with titanium.

297
00:11:33,679 --> 00:11:36,562
Top Gear says the car's structure is

298
00:11:36,562 --> 00:11:38,725
a carbo-titanium monocoque,

299
00:11:38,725 --> 00:11:42,009
with tubular alloy steel subframes at the

300
00:11:42,009 --> 00:11:43,211
front and rear.

301
00:11:43,561 --> 00:11:45,372
Why do forty formulas matter?

302
00:11:45,552 --> 00:11:47,704
Because every part of a car has

303
00:11:47,704 --> 00:11:48,814
a different job.

304
00:11:48,994 --> 00:11:51,193
The part that holds the engine needs

305
00:11:51,193 --> 00:11:51,804
stiffness.

306
00:11:51,984 --> 00:11:54,782
A panel on the nose needs lightness.

307
00:11:54,962 --> 00:11:57,567
A part near the exhaust needs heat

308
00:11:57,567 --> 00:11:58,410
resistance.

309
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:01,487
Using a different recipe for each is

310
00:12:01,487 --> 00:12:03,016
expensive and slow,

311
00:12:03,016 --> 00:12:06,075
which is exactly why mass-made cars do

312
00:12:06,075 --> 00:12:06,880
not do it.

313
00:12:07,230 --> 00:12:10,210
The press release says the monocoque was

314
00:12:10,210 --> 00:12:14,381
entirely redesigned to optimise rigidity and resistance.

315
00:12:14,561 --> 00:12:17,407
And the carbon-titanium monocoque gives,

316
00:12:17,407 --> 00:12:19,044
in the company's words,

317
00:12:19,044 --> 00:12:20,538
an exceptional ratio,

318
00:12:20,538 --> 00:12:22,886
presumably of strength to weight.

319
00:12:23,066 --> 00:12:25,332
We are quoting the company here,

320
00:12:25,332 --> 00:12:27,812
and there is no independent test in

321
00:12:27,812 --> 00:12:28,662
our sources.

322
00:12:29,012 --> 00:12:31,368
There is a history behind this obsession.

323
00:12:31,548 --> 00:12:35,303
Wikipedia says Horacio Pagani formerly created and

324
00:12:35,303 --> 00:12:38,607
managed Lamborghini's composites department,

325
00:12:38,607 --> 00:12:42,587
and in nineteen eighty-eight founded Pagani Composite

326
00:12:42,587 --> 00:12:43,263
Research.

327
00:12:43,443 --> 00:12:46,245
So the man who designed the Utopia

328
00:12:46,245 --> 00:12:49,789
spent decades learning to make carbon fibre

329
00:12:49,789 --> 00:12:52,509
parts, long before he built a car

330
00:12:52,509 --> 00:12:53,416
of his own.

331
00:12:53,766 --> 00:12:55,844
That also explains the weight.

332
00:12:56,024 --> 00:12:59,359
Wikipedia says the Utopia weighs one thousand

333
00:12:59,359 --> 00:13:01,806
two hundred eighty kilograms dry.

334
00:13:01,986 --> 00:13:02,835
The Zonda R,

335
00:13:02,835 --> 00:13:03,968
a track version,

336
00:13:03,968 --> 00:13:05,950
weighs one thousand seventy,

337
00:13:05,950 --> 00:13:08,499
and the first Zonda C twelve weighed

338
00:13:08,499 --> 00:13:10,693
one thousand two hundred fifty.

339
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:12,483
By our own arithmetic,

340
00:13:12,483 --> 00:13:15,630
the Utopia is only thirty kilograms heavier

341
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:18,118
than a nineteen ninety-nine Zonda.

342
00:13:18,468 --> 00:13:20,058
Think about what that means.

343
00:13:20,238 --> 00:13:21,942
In twenty-three years,

344
00:13:21,942 --> 00:13:24,187
the engine got more powerful,

345
00:13:24,187 --> 00:13:25,658
the car got larger,

346
00:13:25,658 --> 00:13:27,671
safety rules got stricter,

347
00:13:27,671 --> 00:13:30,613
and customers wanted air conditioning,

348
00:13:30,613 --> 00:13:32,162
screens and comfort.

349
00:13:32,342 --> 00:13:34,500
Yet the dry weight went up by

350
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,138
only thirty kilograms.

351
00:13:36,318 --> 00:13:38,420
We do not claim this is easy.

352
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,565
We say the sources show that it

353
00:13:40,565 --> 00:13:41,072
is true.

354
00:13:41,423 --> 00:13:44,302
Interior materials follow the same attitude.

355
00:13:44,482 --> 00:13:47,637
The roadster press release lists leather named

356
00:13:47,637 --> 00:13:49,625
